WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:07.259
It's that time of the year where CPAs and
accountants will sit with their clients, entrepreneurs,

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:11.610
and tell them, "Hey, Mr. and Mrs. Entrepreneur,
you should consider giving some money back

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.270
to charity because it benefits you when it
comes down to taxes."

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:19.570
So as much as you do want to give back to
charity because it benefits you tax-wise,

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:22.680
depending on the country you live in, today
I want to talk to you about why you should

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:28.410
consider giving back to the community as an
entrepreneur and how to give back to the community.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.829
So if you're wondering where I'm at right
now, in the background, I'm at Bakersfield

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:34.929
airport, with Mario.

00:00:34.929 --> 00:00:38.300
It is truly one of the smallest airports,
Bakersfield, great city.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:43.140
My buddy back here in a paper plane kid, and
we had to shoot a video because tomorrow is

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.140
a video that's due.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.649
So let me get right into it.

00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:47.800
Listen, there's two ways you give back to
the community.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:48.989
One is money, one is your time.

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:52.620
So why should you consider giving back to
the community?

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.870
There's really five points, and very simple
points on why you should consider giving back

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:56.870
to the community.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:57.870
#1:

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.070
The most important one in my opinion is law
of reciprocity.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:03.159
Let me tell you what's the law of reciprocity.

00:01:03.159 --> 00:01:06.909
I truly believe the more I give, the more
I get in return.

00:01:06.909 --> 00:01:13.009
Not an expectation, I just feel good things
happen to me, the more I give.

00:01:13.009 --> 00:01:15.850
I'm a big believer in the law of reciprocity.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:17.670
I don't know how I'm going to get this thing
in return.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:22.490
Maybe someday someone's going to do something
for my son, my daughter, my family, somebody

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:28.090
close to me that is going to benefit me, but
I believe in the law of reciprocity.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.090
#2

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:33.070
The second benefit that every time I participate
in any kind of way of giving back to the community

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:35.650
is I build so many new relationships.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:36.650
It's very weird.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:41.890
We were just in Hawaii doing something with
Foresters, and we were building a school,

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:44.200
and we were painting some walls.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.439
And I was giving the color pink.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:49.399
I'm painting this chair pink.

00:01:49.399 --> 00:01:50.439
It was hilarious.

00:01:50.439 --> 00:01:54.409
And we made such incredible relationships
with people that we still communicate with

00:01:54.409 --> 00:01:56.270
online.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:58.310
But it doesn't matter what it is.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:02.659
Every single time I've given back to any kind
of charity, there's always been an opportunity

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:04.039
to build new relationships.

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:05.039
#3

00:02:05.039 --> 00:02:07.710
The other part when you give back to charity
is you'll learn a new skill set.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.730
You learn something new, when you're giving
back.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:14.690
There's something that you're learning, whether
that charity, whatever they stand for, you're

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:19.450
learning something about the charity or learning
something that you can benefit yourself.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.160
Maybe they're telling you, "Hey, what we do
is we help families test for this."

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.860
So now you learn about that new skill set.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:26.860
#4

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.950
The fourth one I will tell you would be your
heart.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:34.830
Like your heart gets, I don't know how to
explain this to you.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:41.430
Your heart goes in the mode of giving back,
so it almost becomes gentler, and it gets

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:46.830
in the mood of understanding everybody else's
position in a different way, when you do give

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.780
back, and you're around other people that
want to give back.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.270
So it influences you.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:55.240
If you're somebody that's extremely strong
and rigid, with a military background, charity

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.280
would do very good things to you.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.280
#5

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.270
And fifth point, simple.

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:02.540
Self Esteem.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:04.330
You feel like you're making a difference.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.580
It keeps you grounded.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.380
You feel like the world needs you.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.780
You feel like you are needed in a way.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.690
You realize how incredible of a life you have
as an entrepreneur.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.830
Do give back.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:23.260
So, you know, those five things alone, outside
of the tax benefit, I highly recommend why

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.530
you ought to consider giving back.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:29.400
Now, the question that a lot of people ask
is, "Pat, how do I give back?

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.400
What do I do?"

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:31.740
I got, how many points do I have here, Mario?

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:36.140
I think I wrote 11 points here on how to give
back, and you can pick and choose on how to

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:37.140
do them.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:45.850
So, the first one, we were having a conversation
earlier today at this restaurant.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.180
And I ate some plantains.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:53.120
The plantains were amazing at this place.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.600
It was amazing.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:01.860
We had a great time there.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:06.431
But one of the guys asked me a question, Alejandro
asked me a question and he said, "Hey, what

00:04:06.431 --> 00:04:09.080
do you do when your family starts asking you
for all this money, and they want to borrow

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.870
money and all this other stuff?"

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:15.490
I said, "I don't believe in lending money
to people, especially friends and family."

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:18.090
Because I believe it's the fastest way to
create an enemy.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.590
He said, "What do you mean by that?"

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:27.470
I said, because if you lend money, and you
say yes, they love you, but it's guaranteed

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:30.660
that they're most likely going to come back
and later on ask for what?

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:31.660
More money.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.440
And at some point you have to say what?

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:34.440
No.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.750
So if you give money from yourself to somebody
else, your family's not going to be happy

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.870
that you give money to somebody else, possibly,
if they're lending money.

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:47.350
And then two, if you do loan money to friends
and family, you will typically see them avoiding

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:51.150
you at the next family gathering, and you
feel uncomfortable because you look like you're

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.790
a bill collector, and they kind of don't like
you.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.170
It's just not a fun game to lend money.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:56.170
So I like to give money.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.410
Let me explain to you what I mean by this.

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:01.350
So if somebody asks me, "Pat, can you lend
me $5,000?"

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:06.500
I'll generally say, "No, I won't lend you
$5,000, but I'll give you $300.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.000
You don't ever have to give it back."

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.490
So, they don't like me, they don't hate me.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:14.860
It's a very neutral position, but I gave some
money back, and I'm good to go.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.070
Why?

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:19.810
Because I'm not in the game - I don't think
the biggest benefit is just money being given

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:23.030
away, although money you need to give away,
because some organizations need money to do

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.470
their work that they do.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:25.470
#1

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:29.780
This is why my #1 point on how to give back
is to teach a new skill set.

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:32.050
Teach a new skill set.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:36.300
Go help somebody and give back to your community
by teaching something you're very, very good

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.300
at.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:38.510
Teach somebody else how to do it.

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:39.510
What could that be?

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:40.830
I don't know.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:43.389
How to get ready for a job interview.

00:05:43.389 --> 00:05:45.840
Go and teach people how to be prepared for
a job interview.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.580
Go and sit down with 50 people and tell them,
I'm going to interview you, and you're going

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.110
to know exactly what types of questions you're
going to ask, and I'm going to prepare you

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:54.670
on how to ask those questions.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:55.670
Great.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.400
Give back by teaching people how to put a
resume together.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.720
Give back by sitting down and teaching how
to sell something.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:02.930
Give back by teaching some kind of new skill
set that you have.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:04.530
Social media, whatever it is.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:08.100
But give back to your community by teaching
something you know.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.100
It could be music.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.100
It could be piano.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.100
It could be guitar.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.100
It doesn't matter.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.100
Free lessons for soccer for kids.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.100
It doesn't matter.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:18.170
Somehow, some way, give back and teach a new
skill set, because that lasts.

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:21.730
I think skill set lasts and it generates and
gives them freedom.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:22.730
So #1 is skill set.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:23.730
#2

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.860
Number two is volunteer your time at a hospital
or school.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.860
It's a very easy thing to do.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:32.330
Any time you go to a school and you're giving
back, whether it's Big Brother or you know,

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.200
somebody that needs some kind of help.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:40.260
I've done many, many things with school, where
I was hired to go and, not hired, I didn't

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:41.260
ask for the money.

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.260
It was a LAUSD.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:47.270
I went and spoke to the troubled kids that
had the anklets and they were in prison.

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:51.360
They did time, or they were 13-year-old girls
that were pregnant.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:55.030
Or drug dealers and they put me through a
six month program that I would come down every

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:59.350
other week, and I would take these kids and
we would talk about the biggest thing they

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.350
struggled with.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:05.070
And they would tell me how much they struggle
with pornography or pressure of having sex,

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:09.940
or drugs, or joining gangs, or fights, or
arguments with parents, or what do I do when

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:14.410
my mom and dad, my mom's on drugs, my dad's
on drugs, my parents aren't there, I'm living

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:15.990
on the streets, I'm this, I'm that.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:16.990
All this stuff.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:22.040
And it was one way for them to know that somebody
out there at least cares about them.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:27.130
The reason why that's very important is because
when I was 13 years old, and my parents got

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:32.330
a divorce, and I was a troubled kid, I was
recruited by a basketball league in Echo Park

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.340
called New Century Basketball association.

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:39.180
And they got together all the troubled kids
and gangsters and all this other stuff.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.889
And we played basketball together.

00:07:40.889 --> 00:07:45.311
So that made a very big impact in my life
to know an older man named Vladimir, not an

00:07:45.311 --> 00:07:48.020
older man at that time, he was 20 years older
than me.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:50.730
Vladimir was like an older brother to me.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:53.660
And he gave me direction and hope to know
that somebody believed in me.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.180
That played a very big role in my life.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:08:01.071
So you don't even know who you're going to
be making an impact in their life.

00:08:01.071 --> 00:08:03.610
And one of the simplest ways is hospitals
and schools.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:04.610
#3

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:05.860
Another way is organize a food drive.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:11.600
Mario, I don't know how many times we've done
this, but I remember for many many years when

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:17.120
were in L.A. every Christmas morning at 5:30
in the morning, we'd go to [Mario - Union

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:23.169
Rescue Mission in downtown L.A.], Downtown
L.A. at 5:30 in the morning and we would go

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:29.360
and give away toothpaste, toothbrush, pillows,
towels, and then we'd go to McDonald's and

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:34.669
buy 100, 150 McMuffins and come back and give
food and blankets.

00:08:34.669 --> 00:08:37.079
Another group that would go there would sing
carols to them.

00:08:37.079 --> 00:08:38.919
It was just fascinating.

00:08:38.919 --> 00:08:43.880
Food Drive, because sometimes you'd be amazing
how many people just need a simple meal.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:48.520
Typically, when people come to me and they
tell me, when somebody's begging on the streets

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.639
and they ask me for money, I always offer
food.

00:08:50.639 --> 00:08:51.639
I say, "I'll buy you a meal."

00:08:51.639 --> 00:08:55.639
And if they say, "No, I just want money,"
I don't give them money, because then I know

00:08:55.639 --> 00:08:57.529
what's taking place with the money.

00:08:57.529 --> 00:08:58.529
But I say, "Why do you need money?"

00:08:58.529 --> 00:08:59.529
Oh, because of food.

00:08:59.529 --> 00:09:00.529
Okay, let me go buy you food.

00:09:00.529 --> 00:09:01.529
"Oh, you know what?"

00:09:01.529 --> 00:09:03.160
Then I know exactly where they're at.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:04.379
But if they want me to buy them food, no problem.

00:09:04.379 --> 00:09:05.580
I was in Chicago one night.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.680
It was 1:00 in the morning.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:08.980
I landed, I'm so hungry.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:14.420
I go to this only pub that was open late at
night, and they were offering steak.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:17.540
And this one homeless man outside, he said,
"Can you give me 20 bucks?"

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:20.879
I said, "Man, you're a big thinker if you're
asking for 20 bucks."

00:09:20.879 --> 00:09:22.040
And he said, "Can you give me 20 bucks?"

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.230
I said, "No, but I'll buy you a meal."

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:24.769
He said, "No problem, man.

00:09:24.769 --> 00:09:25.769
I'm so hungry."

00:09:25.769 --> 00:09:26.769
I said, what do you want to have?

00:09:26.769 --> 00:09:27.769
He said anything.

00:09:27.769 --> 00:09:28.769
I said, "Let's have dinner together."

00:09:28.769 --> 00:09:31.041
I take him in the restaurant and the owner
says, "No, he's not welcome here.

00:09:31.041 --> 00:09:32.250
He begs outside all the time."

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.619
I said, "Look, I'm paying."

00:09:33.619 --> 00:09:35.410
He said, "But he can't come inside."

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:36.449
I said, "No problem.

00:09:36.449 --> 00:09:37.629
What do you want to order?"

00:09:37.629 --> 00:09:38.629
Give him a menu.

00:09:38.629 --> 00:09:40.180
He gave him a menu.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.180
And I said, "What do you want?"

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.180
He said, I want a prime rib.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.180
I said, "What else do you want?"

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:44.200
He ordered his food.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.200
So they bring my food.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.200
I could eat it inside.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.399
They didn't let him eat inside.

00:09:48.399 --> 00:09:52.439
I had them serve his prime rib outside to
him, and the drinks outside to him.

00:09:52.439 --> 00:09:54.019
He ate his meal, he was happy.

00:09:54.019 --> 00:09:55.620
I ate, I left.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:57.490
The purpose was served.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:58.649
And I didn't give him money.

00:09:58.649 --> 00:09:59.649
But I did give him food.

00:09:59.649 --> 00:10:03.300
There's many ways you can give back that's
going to help people out.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:04.410
The smallest occasions.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.939
You have no idea how much that means to that
person.

00:10:05.939 --> 00:10:09.529
That person's got a stomach full of food that
night to go to sleep and they're good to go.

00:10:09.529 --> 00:10:10.529
#4

00:10:10.529 --> 00:10:11.600
Fourth way, coach kids.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:14.399
My brother-in-law, I call him a saint.

00:10:14.399 --> 00:10:17.059
I've never met a man like him.

00:10:17.059 --> 00:10:26.230
He is so gentle as a man with kids, that every
parent that he was coaching this summer, the

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:29.999
son, Sean, is like a phenome soccer player.

00:10:29.999 --> 00:10:34.509
He's an absolute beast of a left - he kicks
with his left food, did you know that?

00:10:34.509 --> 00:10:35.509
He's insane.

00:10:35.509 --> 00:10:38.240
I mean, when he plays, the team knows they're
going to win.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:43.660
And so, he was asked by parents after a great
job he did last season, they want him to coach

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:44.660
again.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:45.660
So he went and coached again.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:51.411
And so, one of the ways you can coach is if
you have a good tolerance for kids, and you

00:10:51.411 --> 00:10:55.920
played high school football or baseball or
basketball or soccer and you know the basic

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:59.120
practice tactics because you were a part of
it, give back.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.850
If you've done some organized sports, that's
one of the ways you can do it.

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:02.850
#5

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:04.990
Help raise money for a certain charity or
a foundation.

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:09.920
Just recently we teamed up with Susan G. Komen
for I don't know how many years.

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:14.589
And Jennifer, my wife, is very instrumental
on the way she's working with Susan G. Komen

00:11:14.589 --> 00:11:16.649
and many of the ladies.

00:11:16.649 --> 00:11:19.350
So this time we had many, many events across
the country.

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:22.329
I don't know how many events this was.

00:11:22.329 --> 00:11:24.290
All over the country we did events.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.290
And money was raised.

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:31.160
I mean, it could have been as small as $250
to raising as much as $11,000, $12,000.

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:32.929
And then that money goes to Susan G. Komen.

00:11:32.929 --> 00:11:33.929
Why?

00:11:33.929 --> 00:11:37.949
Well, for them, it could be 68% of the money
is used for research and they're going to

00:11:37.949 --> 00:11:42.410
find out ways for breast cancer, and my grandmother
had breast cancer, and both of them had to

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:46.959
be, you know, and it's a very emotional and
difficult thing a woman goes through.

00:11:46.959 --> 00:11:51.899
And a lot of times you can do simple testing
that, they're educating women on how to test

00:11:51.899 --> 00:11:53.800
- I just think it's very important.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:57.160
So find out what research means a lot to you
and go support that charity.

00:11:57.160 --> 00:12:00.441
There's many of them out there that you can
participate with.

00:12:00.441 --> 00:12:04.379
Go online and look them up and find something
that means a lot to you, and if you're part

00:12:04.379 --> 00:12:07.769
of a company that supports a certain charity,
support them as well.

00:12:07.769 --> 00:12:11.769
But on top of that, be able to support other
charities that mean a lot to you.

00:12:11.769 --> 00:12:14.290
Support those causes as well.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:17.189
#6 is elderly homes.

00:12:17.189 --> 00:12:19.189
Sometimes elderly homes they just want somebody
to talk to them.

00:12:19.189 --> 00:12:22.441
Believe it or not, when you go to elderly
homes, if I can tell you the one question

00:12:22.441 --> 00:12:26.509
to ask when you do go to elderly homes is,
here's my favorite question to ask, "What

00:12:26.509 --> 00:12:31.259
invention was completely crazy when it happened
in your lifetime?"

00:12:31.259 --> 00:12:35.689
And you will have some of the most random
conversations when somebody says, I remember

00:12:35.689 --> 00:12:39.149
when they said this one machine was coming
out, that we were going to watch shows on

00:12:39.149 --> 00:12:40.149
it.

00:12:40.149 --> 00:12:41.149
And it was television.

00:12:41.149 --> 00:12:42.149
How was it?

00:12:42.149 --> 00:12:44.239
Our first person in the city that had it,
it was crazy.

00:12:44.239 --> 00:12:48.769
So when you go there, ask them all sorts of
ways that you can learn from them.

00:12:48.769 --> 00:12:50.579
Hey, I'm a Great Depression baby.

00:12:50.579 --> 00:12:53.490
How was it?

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:54.490
It doesn't matter.

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:59.489
Somebody could be 95 years old and they're
still able to talk and you're sitting there,

00:12:59.489 --> 00:13:00.489
talking to them.

00:13:00.489 --> 00:13:01.970
There's a lot you can give back to them.

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:02.970
So that's elderly.

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:04.870
#7: The next one is give money.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:05.870
It's very simple.

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:08.360
Give money away to different types of things.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:09.739
And one is I talk about research.

00:13:09.739 --> 00:13:15.029
And the other one is giving money away to
certain things that need help.

00:13:15.029 --> 00:13:16.129
It doesn't matter what it is.

00:13:16.129 --> 00:13:20.019
It could be a local community that they're
building a park for kids.

00:13:20.019 --> 00:13:21.019
Great.

00:13:21.019 --> 00:13:22.019
Go contribute for them.

00:13:22.019 --> 00:13:24.220
#8: Then it's building up local businesses.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.959
This is a simple one.

00:13:25.959 --> 00:13:30.389
Find out what local businesses, new local
businesses that got started, and they're just

00:13:30.389 --> 00:13:32.120
kind of trying to get it going.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.730
Help them with their business.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:35.509
Help get the word of mouth out there to help
them out.

00:13:35.509 --> 00:13:36.850
It doesn't matter what it is.

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:40.470
I'm always amazed when people don't want to
support new business owners.

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:42.239
Help that person go out there.

00:13:42.239 --> 00:13:44.920
If they've got good you like, go tell the
world about it.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:48.449
You know, you go to a nice restaurant, even
right now while you're watching this, commit

00:13:48.449 --> 00:13:55.139
today to posting one small business in your
area that just got started that you like.

00:13:55.139 --> 00:13:56.189
It could be a coffee shop.

00:13:56.189 --> 00:13:57.189
It could be a restaurant.

00:13:57.189 --> 00:14:01.769
It could be a gym you go to that's not the
traditional big gym.

00:14:01.769 --> 00:14:04.620
It could be anything that you go to.

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:08.180
Post the link on your Facebook Page, and say
why you like it.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.429
Very simple.

00:14:09.429 --> 00:14:11.920
Post it on Twitter and say why you like it.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:12.920
Simple as that.

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:14.500
It's simple as that on what you need to do.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:15.930
One, tag it to them.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:17.500
They'll be grateful you're doing that.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:22.209
And two, other people will look at you and
say, Man, he or she endorses other small businesses

00:14:22.209 --> 00:14:23.209
and supports other businesses.

00:14:23.209 --> 00:14:24.250
I like his approach.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.701
I'm wondering what he or she does.

00:14:25.701 --> 00:14:27.029
That's you.

00:14:27.029 --> 00:14:29.300
#9 Then we have going big.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.839
I'm a big fan of going big.

00:14:30.839 --> 00:14:34.959
I think you've got to go make tens if not
hundreds millions of dollars.

00:14:34.959 --> 00:14:35.959
Why?

00:14:35.959 --> 00:14:37.259
Because the more money you make, the more
money you can give back.

00:14:37.259 --> 00:14:39.019
So you've got to go big.

00:14:39.019 --> 00:14:42.660
Don't let anybody fool you and tell you that
it's not important to make big money.

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:45.640
If you're a good person, and you're watching
this, and you've got a good heart, and you've

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:47.180
got a giving heart, guess what?

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:48.799
You know what I want people like you to do?

00:14:48.799 --> 00:14:51.360
I want you to make tens of millions of dollars.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:54.480
Because if you make tens of millions of dollars
and you truly have a big heart, you're going

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:55.489
to give lots of money away.

00:14:55.489 --> 00:14:59.290
By the way, if you're somebody watching this,
and you say, I'll give money once I start

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:01.239
making money, no you won't.

00:15:01.239 --> 00:15:05.220
If you're stingy with $10, you're going to
be stingy with $100,000.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:09.279
I guarantee you you'll be stingy with $10
million.

00:15:09.279 --> 00:15:11.639
So just be in the spirit of giving.

00:15:11.639 --> 00:15:16.379
I always remember when one time I was competing
with another guy and he had a nickname of

00:15:16.379 --> 00:15:18.101
being a jerk.

00:15:18.101 --> 00:15:21.290
And one guy got up and he said something very
interesting.

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:22.529
And we were competing hardcore.

00:15:22.529 --> 00:15:23.529
We were good friends.

00:15:23.529 --> 00:15:25.300
But he had this nickname that we'd give him.

00:15:25.300 --> 00:15:28.250
I didn't think he was a jerk, but other people
thought he was a jerk.

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:31.769
And this one guy got up who he didn't like
this competitor.

00:15:31.769 --> 00:15:32.769
And I'm sitting there, there were three of
us.

00:15:32.769 --> 00:15:38.959
And one tried to call him out and the other
guy said, you know what happens when you make

00:15:38.959 --> 00:15:39.959
money?

00:15:39.959 --> 00:15:41.769
Here's all money does to you.

00:15:41.769 --> 00:15:44.550
Money just makes you more of what you are
right now.

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:47.110
If you're a jerk, you're a rich jerk.

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:51.130
If you give a lot right now, you'll give a
lot more when you make more money.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:53.670
It just makes you more of what you are today.

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:54.670
Not much changes.

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:56.560
You just become more of what you are today.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:57.670
So going big.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:59.389
Go and make lots of money.

00:15:59.389 --> 00:16:01.399
Figure out ways how you can contribute to
society.

00:16:01.399 --> 00:16:03.569
#10: The other one is give away books.

00:16:03.569 --> 00:16:05.540
Simply give away books.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:09.709
I don't know how many thousands of books we've
given away.

00:16:09.709 --> 00:16:10.709
5,000?

00:16:10.709 --> 00:16:12.769
I don't know how many thousands of books we've
given way.

00:16:12.769 --> 00:16:15.220
Literally, 5, 6, 7,000 books.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:19.560
Because I feel the same with somebody can
